cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
title: "membrane-propulsion: a synthetic Kuramoto-ring toy with an assumed-law probe and a passive sensor (not propulsion)"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Brisson"
    given-names: "Jean-François"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0000-9778-5374"
    affiliation: "Spark AI NLP, Fredericton, New Brunswick, Canada"
repository-code: "https://github.com/sparkainlp-x/membrane-propulsion"
version: 0.2.0
license: AGPL-3.0-only
abstract: >-
  Synthetic, stdlib-only Python toy: a ring of 64 phase oscillators with a
  travelling drive, a probe whose velocity follows an assumed law
  (proportional to the local phase gradient), and a passive receiver sensor.
  It is not propulsion, not thrust, not a force or energy source and not a
  space drive; no physical claim is made. The repository documents measured
  behaviour and limits, including negative results.
keywords:
  - "synthetic"
  - "toy-model"
  - "kuramoto"
  - "reproducible"
  - "python"
